{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded","id":456427,"title":"Exalted Fiction and Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-24T18:16:54-07:00","id":456427,"title":"Exalted Fiction and Dragon-Blooded","content":"So, i've been reading a lot of the Exalted fiction and novels lately. The Trilogy of the Second Age and a Day Dark as Night and further books... And I've come to notice something very unflattering about the DB's.<br /> <br /> It seems most (not all) of the fiction writers see the Dragon-Blooded as these thug extras. For a simple newly borne Solar to take down an entire Wyld Hunt, and only the Sidereal be any real threat. And not just take them down...take them down easy. An entire Wyld Hunt wasted with 12 arrows. And also, in In Northern Twilight, while it gives pretty impressive details on the visuals of the Terrestrials, they are still just as easily taken down.<br /> <br /> I mean, its pretty lame that one of the Exalted, of any tier, can so easily be tossed aside. They are epic and Chosen and capable of great deeds, with all the heart and fervor of one of the Celestial's. Maybe their power carries a bit less oomph, but that doesn't mean their heroics or import are any less.<br /> <br /> I can understand a certain perspective... a newly Exalted Solar Dawn caste vs a single Dragon-Blood that finds him. Its going to be a tough fight on both ends, the difference being that the Solar will do everything because his life is on the line, and the Dragon-Blooded has the option of withdrawing and contacting his peers, makes the DB less likely to fight to the death, unless he's a Fire Aspect with a ton of pride. But there should be no one-shotting involved at all, at least not just a casual &quot;shot him in the chest with an arrow, he dead&quot;. That's what trained mortal soldiers are for.<br /> <br /> I just hope the fiction for this new edition paints <b>all</b> of the Exalted in the light that they deserve. Terrestrials are not to be trifled with, even by the Celestials, because, believe it or not, they have <i>power.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:19:56-07:00","id":456453,"title":"","content":"Classic Worfing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T06:02:57-07:00","id":456764,"title":"","content":"I have not read any Exalted fiction, but from the sound of it I agree with Zelbinnean; it's Worfing (and extreme one of that). One combat focused Essence 4-5 DB on vacation would be a very scary opponent for a newish Solar. The same DB fully geared for a Wyld hunt... Then add the rest of the hunt members... Even with 2nd editions power tiers between the different Exalts, a &quot;newly borne Solar to take down an entire Wyld Hunt&quot; sounds like bad writing no matter how second rate the hunt in question is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T07:25:02-07:00","id":456819,"title":"","content":"This perception was not helped very much at all by Dragon-Blooded mechanical performance in 1e and pre-errata 2e. Without powerful stacked defences (1e) and cheap perfects (2e) Dragon-Bloods would fall against even moderately experienced Solars and Celestials as though they were nothing. <br /> <br /> 2.5 errata has redressed the balance somewhat. I've had Dragon-Bloods fight similarly experienced Celestials to a standstill and even scored some wins, which would previously have been unthinkable. Group defences, cooperative attacks, buffs and coordination Charms make well integrated parties of Dragon-Bloods a significant threat. They still have some technical issues such as some Abilities being very weak in comparison to others, but overall they are much more robust. <br /> <br /> The only third edition fiction featuring Dragon-Bloods we have so far are from the anthology. Although the only Wyld Hunt that appears is defeated, they are treated as a serious threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T07:29:30-07:00","id":456832,"title":"","content":"I agree with crumple with the caveat that the narrative, particular fiction, should not feel beholden to game mechanics as a prerequisite for writing a good story. It's non-interactive, unlike an RPG - nobody gets hurt if DBs seem to be narratively tougher in fiction than they really were in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T07:36:43-07:00","id":456837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=456832#post456832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with crumple with the caveat that the narrative, particular fiction, should not feel beholden to game mechanics as a prerequisite for writing a good story. It's non-interactive, unlike an RPG - nobody gets hurt if DBs seem to be narratively tougher in fiction than they really were in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I agree with the caveat, I meant only that the mechanical problems contributed to the perception. I remember Dragon-Bloods being spoken of as extras more than once. This clearly wasn't in line with the writer intent; I think it was Grabowski who said he intended Mnemon to be one of the primary antagonists of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:02:00-07:00","id":456872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=456819#post456819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This perception was not helped very much at all by Dragon-Blooded mechanical performance in 1e and pre-errata 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kidding, right? You're pulling some kind of elaborate joke?<br /> <br /> Pre-errata, Essence Disruption Attack was a non-Shaping non-attack that could tack on an arbitrary number of motes to the cost of your so-called &quot;cheap&quot; perfects, and once that happened, they could tag you with the non-Shaping Soul Mastery to destroy your soul and kill you dead. Easy access to jade and not having to pay double for the bonus and no clause against stacking also meant they could lay into you with extremely low-Speed attacks and have their DV refresh twice for every time you act.<br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> some mechanical holes, but DBs being able to beat Solars was <b>not</b> something that was invented with the first batch of errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:08:18-07:00","id":456876,"title":"","content":"What does Worfing means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:17:00-07:00","id":456880,"title":"","content":"From Star Trek: TNG. Showing how strong someone is by beating up the Character named Worf, that was supposed to be a stong warrior.<br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheWorfEffect\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph.../TheWorfEffect</a><br /> I haven't read it (or perhaps did back then, but forgot it...), but here is an older thread here about it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/84088-worfing-and-the-exalted-good-or-bad\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ed-good-or-bad</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:37:33-07:00","id":456970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=456872#post456872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-errata, Essence Disruption Attack was a non-Shaping non-attack that could tack on an arbitrary number of motes to the cost of your so-called &quot;cheap&quot; perfects, and once that happened, they could tag you with the non-Shaping Soul Mastery to destroy your soul and kill you dead. Easy access to jade and not having to pay double for the bonus and no clause against stacking also meant they could lay into you with extremely low-Speed attacks and have their DV refresh twice for every time you act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence Disruption Attack could only tack on an arbitrary number of motes to cheap perfects if it was not itself overcome by a cheap perfect. Having deleterious effects on the target's traits qualified it as an attack under 2e. EDA cost 3m+ 1wp, and could, like any other attack, be blocked for 3m by Seven Shadow Evasion. Soul Mastery was a terrible Charm because not only was it very expensive (10m), but when it was perfected for (Essence) actions it would kill the Immaculate instead.<br /> <br /> That was perfect-or-die gameplay in action. Every attack that could possibly threaten you got perfected. In 2e DBs did not have cheap all-applicable perfect defences and therefore they would lose combat with Solars every time.<br /> <br /> 2.5 fixed the worst of it and that should be celebrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-25-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:40:58-07:00","id":456973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=456872#post456872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're kidding, right? You're pulling some kind of elaborate joke?<br /> <br /> Pre-errata, Essence Disruption Attack was a non-Shaping non-attack that could tack on an arbitrary number of motes to the cost of your so-called &quot;cheap&quot; perfects, and once that happened, they could tag you with the non-Shaping Soul Mastery to destroy your soul and kill you dead. Easy access to jade and not having to pay double for the bonus and no clause against stacking also meant they could lay into you with extremely low-Speed attacks and have their DV refresh twice for every time you act.<br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> some mechanical holes, but DBs being able to beat Solars was <b>not</b> something that was invented with the first batch of errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple powerful Charms do not a good Charmset make. I consider the vast majority of DB Charms to be on the Sidereal level of &quot;usability&quot; or &quot;interacts appropriately with the 2e system.&quot;<br /> <br /> Copypasta + 1e conversions done by people who didn't remotely understand the 2nd edition rules made for truly shitty mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:20:27-07:00","id":457132,"title":"","content":"It's somewhat unfortunate but I find this unlikely to change. DBs play the role of jobber really really well. They roll in, hold a daiklave to your throat, demand all your money, and then use it to buy coke and snort it of your now enslaved sister. There's enough of them that killing a few isn't a big deal and the realm is big enough to take the hit. They're also everywhere and you don't need an excuse for them to be fighting because...well Wyld Hunt. In theory DBs are bad assets, theres lots of them, they work well in teams, they're covered in magic weapons and armor, and their powers are really flashy to look at and describe. It takes a whole lot of worfing to make a blazing hero, wielding the relic blade of his ancestors, forged in the dying embers of the First Flame, surrounded by his zealous sworn brothers and their mortal soldiers into a chump.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm hoping they vary it up a bit in the next edition. I think there's zero chance that they'll start depicting successful Wyld Hunts, but switching up who gets beat on to prove X is a badass would be cool. Right now Lunars and DBs get the short end of the stick all the time. It's just starting to have an adverse effect where I see elemental samurai in glittering Jade armor and I just wonder what pillar the dawn is going to throw them through to show off what a boss he is. <br /> <br /> Solars are the heroes of all the books/comics in exalted, to the best of my recollection anyway, so you can't really have them lose. Then you'd have no more heroes. The DBs and Lunars could stand to be a little more cool while they lose though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:43:16-07:00","id":457204,"title":"","content":"I dunno. Depicting various stories where the Wyld Hunt did succeed would go a long way to showing &quot;Hey, a Wyld Hunt. Unless you're VERY resourceful and just damn lucky, you're probably gonna die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Naturally, PC's get very luck by way of the ST, but the Wyld Hunt has been tremendously successful throughout the years. Showcasing a few of their more exciting take downs I think would be just swell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:55:28-07:00","id":457219,"title":"","content":"I am not well versed on 2nd edition but I remember a few examples of Solars losing in the chapter fiction, Dace is beaten by Ma Ha Suchi, a solar boy is killed by Cynis Avaku etc. Maybe I don't interact enough with the sound chamber of these forums but a lot of the solar hate I see seems to ignore any of the many stories that have the solars running for their lives or losing. I'm not saying db's and lunar's don't get the short end of it but I have a hard time taking posts like this seriously. The book was written with the purposes of having the solars be the hero's obviously they are going to be the badassest of all. Conan seldom struggles one against one with even well trained soldiers. Whether A dragonblooded should by definition be a big bad that gets a lot of page count should vary by the needs of the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/401-urgenthal","name":"Urgenthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:56:27-07:00","id":457220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457204#post457204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. Depicting various stories where the Wyld Hunt did succeed would go a long way to showing &quot;Hey, a Wyld Hunt. Unless you're VERY resourceful and just damn lucky, you're probably gonna die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Naturally, PC's get very luck by way of the ST, but the Wyld Hunt has been tremendously successful throughout the years. Showcasing a few of their more exciting take downs I think would be just swell.</div> </div> </div> </div>i agree so far the only times iv'e seen a db take down a celestial exalt was when A it was a freaking kid, way to show of the dragon blooded power there. B by using the dawn to punch the heck out of the eclipse whilst cool it doesn't really make up for the fact that the other db's where killed ridiculously easy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:01:51-07:00","id":457235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urgenthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457219#post457219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not well versed on 2nd edition but I remember a few examples of Solars losing in the chapter fiction, Dace is beaten by Ma Ha Suchi, a solar boy is killed by Cynis Avaku etc. Maybe I don't interact enough with the sound chamber of these forums but a lot of the solar hate I see seems to ignore any of the many stories that have the solars running for their lives or losing. I'm not saying db's and lunar's don't get the short end of it but I have a hard time taking posts like this seriously. The book was written with the purposes of having the solars be the hero's obviously they are going to be the badassest of all. Conan seldom struggles one against one with even well trained soldiers. Whether A dragonblooded should by definition be a big bad that gets a lot of page count should vary by the needs of the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not that it never happens. Sure, like you said, there are examples of the Solars being bested by the likes of DB's and Lunars...but they are <i><b>extremely</b></i> sparse.<br /> <br /> And of course, the game line does introduce the Solars as the primary protagonists, so they're going to win more often than not. That said, to completely demean another Exalt type by, for example, having a single newly born Solar kill an entire Wyld Hunt of Dragon Bloods and defeat a hundreds year old Sidereal with 12 hand-made arrows and a dagger, very easily mind you, is going too far.<br /> <br /> If you look through most of the fiction, Terrestials get (and I hate this phrase) curb stomped at every opportunity. Its just not right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:04:19-07:00","id":457236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457220#post457220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i agree so far the only times iv'e seen a db take down a celestial exalt was when A it was a freaking kid, way to show of the dragon blooded power there. B by using the dawn to punch the heck out of the eclipse whilst cool it doesn't really make up for the fact that the other db's where killed ridiculously easy</div> </div> </div> </div>Just accept that the eclipse caste mark is the mark of death, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:07:39-07:00","id":457242,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me but I usually find that the curb stomping in the fiction happens to whoever the fiction is not following. Heysha Black Asp handles Harmonious Jade with mocking ease in the comic they share. It seems to me that if the comic/fiction is showing off one of the exalt types whoever is up against them is getting smashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/401-urgenthal","name":"Urgenthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:13:20-07:00","id":457244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457132#post457132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I'm hoping they vary it up a bit in the next edition. I think there's zero chance that they'll start depicting successful Wyld Hunts, but switching up who gets beat on to prove X is a badass would be cool. Right now Lunars and DBs get the short end of the stick all the time. It's just starting to have an adverse effect where I see elemental samurai in glittering Jade armor and I just wonder what pillar the dawn is going to throw them through to show off what a boss he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if absolutely nowhere else -- and I'd seriously question <i>that</i> -- depicting instances of Terrestrials and Lunars <i>in their own books</i> sometimes finding legitimate success against Solars seems imminently reasonable. It really is just a matter of holding writers to not depicting things in a completely lazy and nuance-free manner. Even in cases where the non-Solar loses, sticking to this policy will avoid making the non-Solar look consistently like a chump.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Solars are the heroes of all the books/comics in exalted, to the best of my recollection anyway, so you can't really have them lose. Then you'd have no more heroes. The DBs and Lunars could stand to be a little more cool while they lose though. </div> </div> </div>Even within the situation you've framed, there's room for non-Solar characters winning against <i>other</i> Solar characters in the book. More than that, all fights needn't end with one or both participants dead: a Solar protagonist can know defeat at the hands of a non-Solar without meaning the book is over. Hell, such a Solar protagonist doesn't even need to have and win in a rematch later on to &quot;make up for it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:36:03-07:00","id":457257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457236#post457236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just accept that the eclipse caste mark is the mark of death, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>jupp we got the sun, the pancake, the smily, the circle and the target... so have fun guys and gals with a target on your foreheads","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T14:24:45-07:00","id":457280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urgenthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457219#post457219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not well versed on 2nd edition but I remember a few examples of Solars losing in the chapter fiction, Dace is beaten by Ma Ha Suchi, a solar boy is killed by Cynis Avaku etc. Maybe I don't interact enough with the sound chamber of these forums but a lot of the solar hate I see seems to ignore any of the many stories that have the solars running for their lives or losing. I'm not saying db's and lunar's don't get the short end of it but I have a hard time taking posts like this seriously. The book was written with the purposes of having the solars be the hero's obviously they are going to be the badassest of all. Conan seldom struggles one against one with even well trained soldiers. Whether A dragonblooded should by definition be a big bad that gets a lot of page count should vary by the needs of the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look let's be real.<br /> <br /> If an elder Lunar can't reasonably beat a relatively-new Solar, some dumb shit is happening.<br /> <br /> If an experienced DB can't reasonably beat a brand-new Solar (and a noncombat-focused one at that), some dumb shit is happening.<br /> <br /> Also your premise is flawed. In a hypothetical Conan RPG, those soldiers are not going to be PC types. When most art and fiction depicts DBs, <i>a splat designed to be played</i>, as utter chumps...there are problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T14:59:42-07:00","id":457338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457204#post457204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. Depicting various stories where the Wyld Hunt did succeed would go a long way to showing &quot;Hey, a Wyld Hunt. Unless you're VERY resourceful and just damn lucky, you're probably gonna die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Naturally, PC's get very luck by way of the ST, but the Wyld Hunt has been tremendously successful throughout the years. Showcasing a few of their more exciting take downs I think would be just swell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the same time though, you don't want the Wyld Hunt coming across as <i>too</i> overwhelming powerful or dangerous, because then ST's may feel that these hardcore Wyld Hunts are normal ones, and that if they need to make the Wyld Hunt so dangerous that they end up with a bunch of dead PCs. <br /> <br /> It's definitely a tricky road to walk. I think we can agree that the fiction didn't do a very good job of walking that road in 1st and 2nd edition, and can only hope that 3rd edition does a better job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:05:28-07:00","id":457344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457338#post457338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time though, you don't want the Wyld Hunt coming across as <i>too</i> overwhelming powerful or dangerous, because then ST's may feel that these hardcore Wyld Hunts are normal ones, and that if they need to make the Wyld Hunt so dangerous that they end up with a bunch of dead PCs.<br /> <br /> It's definitely a tricky road to walk. I think we can agree that the fiction didn't do a very good job of walking that road in 1st and 2nd edition, and can only hope that 3rd edition does a better job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fiction aside, 3e explicitly repudiating the previous rocket-tag combat models means it's less likely for PCs to just be up and dead.<br /> <br /> Though I know a few players who would rather die fighting than <i>ever</i> withdraw from a superior force. But that's on them, not the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:18:27-07:00","id":457351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457344#post457344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fiction aside, 3e explicitly repudiating the previous rocket-tag combat models means it's less likely for PCs to just be up and dead.<br /> <br /> Though I know a few players who would rather die fighting than <i>ever</i> withdraw from a superior force. But that's on them, not the system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My point is, you don't want the gameline presenting the Wyld Hunt as <i>too</i> overwhelmingly powerful, just as you don't want it to present the Hunt as a joke. There needs to be some level of balance in there, and I hope 3rd edition hits that a lot better than the last two did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:26:44-07:00","id":457354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457351#post457351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My point is, you don't want the gameline presenting the Wyld Hunt as <i>too</i> overwhelmingly powerful, just as you don't want it to present the Hunt as a joke. There needs to be some level of balance in there, and I hope 3rd edition hits that a lot better than the last two did.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe some sort of &quot;hunt levels&quot; like maybe a first circle hunt will be made up of a relatively &quot;green&quot; sworn brotherhood and a force of soldiers that is meant to go after free willed first and possibly second circle demons, greedy minor gods, rampaging loner fairfolk nobles and the likes whilst a third circle hunt is more or less one or more legions equipped with the best and containing multiple elite brotherhoods and well they are meant to go after the REALLY bad stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:34:29-07:00","id":457362,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Wyld Hunt can vary wildly. It could be composed of 3 local, outcaste Dragon Blooded who aren't terribly experienced and got together to go kill the Anathema. Or it could be composed of multiple legions of crack soldiers coupled by brotherhoods of Immaculate monks and then backed up with powerful artifacts, sorcerers, demons and Sidereal. <br /> <br /> In general, you probably won't want to bring out the latter until end game against your players. But you have to be careful with the former, because too many of those and Dragon Blooded will just look like chumps. <br /> <br /> The big problem is that the last &quot;super&quot; Wyld Hunt got its ass kicked by the Bull of the North. So Dragon Blooded are <i>already</i> looking a little chumpy because their &quot;ultimate Wyld Hunt&quot; was utterly crushed. Plus you had all kinds of bullshit in the books reminding you that Terrestrial Exalted barely qualified as Exalted at all. Fuck that.<br /> <br /> Anyway... yeah... not sure where exactly I'm going with this. I guess I just hope 3rd edition sets a better tone for Dragon Blooded and they don't end up coming across as chumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:39:27-07:00","id":457368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457351#post457351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, you don't want the gameline presenting the Wyld Hunt as <i>too</i> overwhelmingly powerful, just as you don't want it to present the Hunt as a joke. There needs to be some level of balance in there, and I hope 3rd edition hits that a lot better than the last two did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think PCs should always be scared of what the Wyld Hunt <i>could</i> bring down if they attract too much attention and the Hunt orients directly at them, rather than just <i>what they are likely </i>to bring to bear in the immediate area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T16:50:20-07:00","id":457419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457362#post457362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Wyld Hunt can vary wildly. It could be composed of 3 local, outcaste Dragon Blooded who aren't terribly experienced and got together to go kill the Anathema. Or it could be composed of multiple legions of crack soldiers coupled by brotherhoods of Immaculate monks and then backed up with powerful artifacts, sorcerers, demons and Sidereal.<br /> <br /> In general, you probably won't want to bring out the latter until end game against your players. But you have to be careful with the former, because too many of those and Dragon Blooded will just look like chumps.<br /> <br /> The big problem is that the last &quot;super&quot; Wyld Hunt got its ass kicked by the Bull of the North. So Dragon Blooded are <i>already</i> looking a little chumpy because their &quot;ultimate Wyld Hunt&quot; was utterly crushed. Plus you had all kinds of bullshit in the books reminding you that Terrestrial Exalted barely qualified as Exalted at all. Fuck that.<br /> <br /> Anyway... yeah... not sure where exactly I'm going with this. I guess I just hope 3rd edition sets a better tone for Dragon Blooded and they don't end up coming across as chumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>wasn't one of the big reasons the tepet hunt failed because that stupid disgrace of db Lisara and because the regent Fokuf more or less betrayed the tepet legions and sent them to their doom without proper supply lines and stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:15:05-07:00","id":457482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457419#post457419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wasn't one of the big reasons the tepet hunt failed because that stupid disgrace of db Lisara and because the regent Fokuf more or less betrayed the tepet legions and sent them to their doom without proper supply lines and stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That wasn't a Hunt, but a full deployment of legions for war.<br /> <br /> The Hunt is a very different thing, a different institution from the army, and it engages threats in a more PC fashion (I have played in, and seen played, a few Wyld Hunt games), with a small group of badasses finding and neutralizing a threat, rather than being in an all-out war with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attach