s-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:09:53-07:00","id":457541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457530#post457530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm it's the first time I've heard that name (i think) who or what is Samea?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Zenith caste sorceress and second to Yurgen.<br /> <br /> She provided a crucial advantage against the Tepet campaign by binding Second Circle Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-25-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:10:19-07:00","id":457544,"title":"","content":"She's the Celestial Circle sorceress Zenith that he's allied himself with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:11:17-07:00","id":457545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457530#post457530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm it's the first time I've heard that name (i think) who or what is Samea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Zenith Caste Solar Sorceress in the Bull of the North's circle who is older than him and seems to be the one responsible for how his armies go all over the place with no regard for logistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:22:59-07:00","id":457548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded#post456427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i've been reading a lot of the Exalted fiction and novels lately. The Trilogy of the Second Age and a Day Dark as Night and further books... And I've come to notice something very unflattering about the DB's.<br /> <br /> It seems most (not all) of the fiction writers see the Dragon-Blooded as these thug extras. For a simple newly borne Solar to take down an entire Wyld Hunt, and only the Sidereal be any real threat. And not just take them down...take them down easy. An entire Wyld Hunt wasted with 12 arrows. And also, in In Northern Twilight, while it gives pretty impressive details on the visuals of the Terrestrials, they are still just as easily taken down.<br /> <br /> I mean, its pretty lame that one of the Exalted, of any tier, can so easily be tossed aside. They are epic and Chosen and capable of great deeds, with all the heart and fervor of one of the Celestial's. Maybe their power carries a bit less oomph, but that doesn't mean their heroics or import are any less.<br /> <br /> I can understand a certain perspective... a newly Exalted Solar Dawn caste vs a single Dragon-Blood that finds him. Its going to be a tough fight on both ends, the difference being that the Solar will do everything because his life is on the line, and the Dragon-Blooded has the option of withdrawing and contacting his peers, makes the DB less likely to fight to the death, unless he's a Fire Aspect with a ton of pride. But there should be no one-shotting involved at all, at least not just a casual &quot;shot him in the chest with an arrow, he dead&quot;. That's what trained mortal soldiers are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the simplest answer is likely the most accurate here. Those fictions you're reading are about Solars, so of course they're gonna beat any DBs they happen to fight. It's a pretty crappy story if you kill the protagonist 3-4 chapters into the book. I'd also like to point out that most of those books do not accurately represent a true Wyld Hunt. The MoEP: DBs implied that a typical Wyld Hunt usually included at a minimum of something like 5-6 DBs (at least one of them an Immaculate MA) and anywhere from 50-200 mortals. I believe the novel &quot;In Northern Twilight&quot; had a primary group of just 5 DBs and the leader mentioned that their numbers were significantly reduced. So several of the Wyld Hunts in those novels were very poorly represented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded#post456427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope the fiction for this new edition paints <b>all</b> of the Exalted in the light that they deserve. Terrestrials are not to be trifled with, even by the Celestials, because, believe it or not, they have <i>power.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>As for this statement, the Devs have said that while the power gap between splats has been reduced, that it does still exist. Solar's are still the strongest and DB's are still the weakest (that we have knowledge of anyways). I'm not saying a Solar is going to walk over a dozen DBs, it'd be suicidal to try really. A beginning Solar is likely to hold his own against 2-3 beginning DBs though. Terrestrial's have always won such battles by numbers. There isn't anything wrong with that either. In a fair open fight, the 20,000 DBs in Creation right now could trounce all 300 Solars, 400+ Lunars, and 100 Sidereals at the same time. Now imagine what they could do if they got their numbers back up to the pre-Contagion days when they had 900,000+ Terrestrials. That's a military force without equal!<br /> <br /> Caveat: It is always possible for a DB to kill a Solar even in single combat. It depends on their individuals specs and what happened that led up to the confrontation. It's also possible for a mortal to kill a Solar or a DB as well. The Devs have said they went through some serious alterations to make sure it was possible for even the underdogs to win a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 03-25-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:38:06-07:00","id":457566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457548#post457548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the simplest answer is likely the most accurate here. Those fictions you're reading are about Solars, so of course they're gonna beat any DBs they happen to fight. It's a pretty crappy story if you kill the protagonist 3-4 chapters into the book. I'd also like to point out that most of those books do not accurately represent a true Wyld Hunt. The MoEP: DBs implied that a typical Wyld Hunt usually included at a minimum of something like 5-6 DBs (at least one of them an Immaculate MA) and anywhere from 50-200 mortals. I believe the novel &quot;In Northern Twilight&quot; had a primary group of just 5 DBs and the leader mentioned that their numbers were significantly reduced. So several of the Wyld Hunts in those novels were very poorly represented.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for this statement, the Devs have said that while the power gap between splats has been reduced, that it does still exist. Solar's are still the strongest and DB's are still the weakest (that we have knowledge of anyways). I'm not saying a Solar is going to walk over a dozen DBs, it'd be suicidal to try really. A beginning Solar is likely to hold his own against 2-3 beginning DBs though. Terrestrial's have always won such battles by numbers. There isn't anything wrong with that either. In a fair open fight, the 20,000 DBs in Creation right now could trounce all 300 Solars, 400+ Lunars, and 100 Sidereals at the same time. Now imagine what they could do if they got their numbers back up to the pre-Contagion days when they had 900,000+ Terrestrials. That's a military force without equal!<br /> <br /> Caveat: It is always possible for a DB to kill a Solar even in single combat. It depends on their individuals specs and what happened that led up to the confrontation. It's also possible for a mortal to kill a Solar or a DB as well. The Devs have said they went through some serious alterations to make sure it was possible for even the underdogs to win a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>where did the 100 extra lunars come from? also wohooo for DB's not being canon fodder glorified extras anymore","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:45:50-07:00","id":457574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457566#post457566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where did the 100 extra lunars come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs said that in EX3, there are &quot;around 400&quot; Lunars. There is no strict equivalency between numbers of Solars and numbers of Lunars any longer. The significance or reason for that unspecified number remains to be seen!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also wohooo for DB's not being canon fodder glorified extras anymore </div> </div> </div>Yea, verily. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:52:25-07:00","id":457577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457574#post457574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs said that in EX3, there are &quot;around 400&quot; Lunars. There is no strict equivalency between numbers of Solars and numbers of Lunars any longer. The significance or reason for that unspecified number remains to be seen!<br /> <br /> Yea, verily. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>... well that kind of wrecks my whole image of lunars completely so i'm just going to ignore that change since it kinda makes lunars feel less significant than solars in my opinion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:08:37-07:00","id":457581,"title":"","content":"OP: A disappointing trend in fiction can (and should) be reversed without erring in the absolute opposite direction. I promise you there are Exalts who have died the moment battle started, and some before they even realized there was a fight. If that can happen to a Solar (and it can) it can happen to anyone.<br /> <br /> Best is if writers don't assume one form of storytelling for every case. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:44:17-07:00","id":457639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457577#post457577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... well that kind of wrecks my whole image of lunars completely so i'm just going to ignore that change since it kinda makes lunars feel less significant than solars in my opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question, do you consider Sidereals more significant than Solars because there are fewer of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T20:07:28-07:00","id":457649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457639#post457639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious question, do you consider Sidereals more significant than Solars because there are fewer of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to speak for Xanroth, but it could be that the &quot;whole image of Lunars&quot; alluded to has more to do with valuing the sun-moon dualism. I would be interested in hearing more about why it strikes Xanroth as so ruinous to their significance, though.<br /> <br /> There are different ways to gauge &quot;significance,&quot; after all. By one measure, it shouldn't <i>make</i> Lunars less significant than Solars because they and all other Exalt types have <i>always</i> been regarded as less significant than Solars as a group, to whatever degree that matters. By another, the numbers are irrelevant: EX3's Lunars are as significant as Solars because both actually have legitimately meaningful places in the setting, instead of having been shoehorned in at the eleventh hour like the Lunars of 1e and 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T23:56:21-07:00","id":457806,"title":"","content":"To note, my aggravation isn't with the power tier. I understand and actually like the power schism between Exalt types. Its cool that a Solar is stronger than a Dragon-Blooded, its built right into the theme of the game.<br /> <br /> A Solar taking out multiple Dragon-Blooded can and does happen, and thats ok. Whats not ok, in my opinion, is the Dragon-Bloods being treated like extras and the Solar just carving through them like butter. Especially newborns verses multiple experienced ones. Even for a trained Solar, a trained Dragon-Blood is <i>still </i>a threat, and the danger only increases the more that there are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457581#post457581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP: A disappointing trend in fiction can (and should) be reversed without erring in the absolute opposite direction. I promise you there are Exalts who have died the moment battle started, and some before they even realized there was a fight. If that can happen to a Solar (and it can) it can happen to anyone.<br /> <br /> Best is if writers don't assume one form of storytelling for every case.</div> </div> </div> </div>:.D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T01:34:45-07:00","id":457830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457649#post457649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to speak for Xanroth, but it could be that the &quot;whole image of Lunars&quot; alluded to has more to do with valuing the sun-moon dualism. I would be interested in hearing more about why it strikes Xanroth as so ruinous to their significance, though.<br /> <br /> There are different ways to gauge &quot;significance,&quot; after all. By one measure, it shouldn't <i>make</i> Lunars less significant than Solars because they and all other Exalt types have <i>always</i> been regarded as less significant than Solars as a group, to whatever degree that matters. By another, the numbers are irrelevant: EX3's Lunars are as significant as Solars because both actually have legitimately meaningful places in the setting, instead of having been shoehorned in at the eleventh hour like the Lunars of 1e and 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you its more or less what you said there i was pretty tired when i wrote that and i get aggravated easily when i'm tired.<br /> What i find so damn destructive about that change is that i always loved that whole one specific lunar shares a powerful bond with one specific solar.<br /> That together the two of them these two fantastic beings possessing unbelievable powers &quot;completed&quot; each others becoming able to overcome any and all obstacles.<br /> But now it seems like that's out the window along with the whole notion that the lunars where made as &quot;equals&quot; to the solars just in a different manner and the whole bond thing was because US could not stand having anything be considered equal to anything he does (bloody US deserves a slap in the face for that attitude).<br /> Now it feels like if there is a bond then it will be less significant than before or if it's like before then suddenly instead of one solar and one lunar it feels like it would<br /> Become something like one solar and a bloody lunar harem more or less.<br /> That's my reasoning i hope i make sense...<br /> P.S. i do kind of prefer sidis over solars but that's because they can reduce the difficulty on dice rolls and boy do the dice HATE me (32 dice and i botch it doesn't get much worse than that)<br /> <br /> also i apologize about the text wall but i'm still a bit tired and my syndromes makes it hard to do the grammar correctly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 03-26-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T02:07:16-07:00","id":457857,"title":"","content":"I guess writing narrow escapes, conflict avoidance, and guerilla tacticts are lost arts to some authors.<br /> <br /> Want to have a Solar and don't have to dodge the attention of the Realm all of the time? Focus on a Solar in a far away place generally ignored; like the Bull. When the news reach anyone able to send a Wyld Hunt or a Legion, it isn't about a newly exalted Solar without allies and resources anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T04:01:41-07:00","id":457879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded#post456427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, i've been reading a lot of the Exalted fiction and novels lately. The Trilogy of the Second Age and a Day Dark as Night and further books... And I've come to notice something very unflattering about the DB's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in <i>A Day Dark as Night</i>, Risa puts up a decent fight against Harmonious Jade. <br /> <br /> In <i>In Northern Twilight</i> the circle faced by newly exalted Swan and Arianna were quite disfunctional, and apparently set up to fall by Gold Faction manipulation, as was Magistrate Gerik when challenged Swan later. <br /> <br /> The 'false' wild hunt Swan faced in <i>A Shadow Over Heavens Eye</i> was a bit more of a challenge, but it was also established to be less than optimal.<br /> <br /> However, the hunt lead by Holok against young Yushuv in <i>Chosen of the Sun</i> had no such excuses. They were totally Worfed to show how bad-arsed Yushuv had become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T05:04:47-07:00","id":457952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457830#post457830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you its more or less what you said there i was pretty tired when i wrote that and i get aggravated easily when i'm tired.<br /> What i find so damn destructive about that change is that i always loved that whole one specific lunar shares a powerful bond with one specific solar.<br /> That together the two of them these two fantastic beings possessing unbelievable powers &amp;quot;completed&amp;quot; each others becoming able to overcome any and all obstacles.<br /> But now it seems like that's out the window along with the whole notion that the lunars where made as &amp;quot;equals&amp;quot; to the solars just in a different manner and the whole bond thing was because US could not stand having anything be considered equal to anything he does (bloody US deserves a slap in the face for that attitude).<br /> Now it feels like if there is a bond then it will be less significant than before or if it's like before then suddenly instead of one solar and one lunar it feels like it would<br /> Become something like one solar and a bloody lunar harem more or less.<br /> That's my reasoning i hope i make sense...<br /> P.S. i do kind of prefer sidis over solars but that's because they can reduce the difficulty on dice rolls and boy do the dice HATE me (32 dice and i botch it doesn't get much worse than that)<br /> <br /> also i apologize about the text wall but i'm still a bit tired and my syndromes makes it hard to do the grammar correctly</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I find the idea that every Lunar needs a Solar soulmate to be &quot;complete&quot; to be seriously vile. If any one idea ever expressed about the setting damages the &quot;significance&quot; of Lunars, I believe it's this one.<br /> <br /> Resisting Meerkat Steals the Spotlight, though - balancing correct portrayal of Dragon-Blooded conflict with Solars and Lunars is tricky. You don't want to paint the Dragon-Blooded as irresistible foes, almost as powerful and with many times the numbers and resources as Solar or Lunar PCs, because that just leads to dead PCs. Conversely, if they can't offer a threat at all, what's the point? Tricky, artful balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T05:09:46-07:00","id":457954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457952#post457952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I find the idea that every Lunar needs a Solar soulmate to be &quot;complete&quot; to be seriously vile. If any one idea ever expressed about the setting damages the &quot;significance&quot; of Lunars, I believe it's this one.<br /> <br /> Resisting Meerkat Steals the Spotlight, though - balancing correct portrayal of Dragon-Blooded conflict with Solars and Lunars is tricky. You don't want to paint the Dragon-Blooded as irresistible foes, almost as powerful and with many times the numbers and resources as Solar or Lunar PCs, because that just leads to dead PCs. Conversely, if they can't offer a threat at all, what's the point? Tricky, artful balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>nonononono i did not mean that the lunar needed it i meant that the SOLARS needed the balancing force that the lunars brings to eeer i can't for whatever reason remember the word i'm looking for but complete was the closest i could remember so lets go with that each others getting the assistance from their partner when their &quot;i am the best at X but can't do jack about other stuff&quot; ideology doesn't work. i hope i make sense and yes i apologize about the lunar talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T05:48:45-07:00","id":457962,"title":"","content":"Well if there are 300 Solars and 400 Lunars, maybe all the Solars have mates but the Lunars don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T06:09:59-07:00","id":457970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457962#post457962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if there are 300 Solars and 400 Lunars, maybe all the Solars have mates but the Lunars don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not even that.<br /> <br /> The new Lunar Bond will not be something constructed into all exaltations, but something added to some of them by bearers with an intense relationship.<br /> <br /> It's an option, not a requirement.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457830#post457830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now it feels like if there is a bond then it will be less significant than before or if it's like before then suddenly instead of one solar and one lunar it feels like it would<br /> Become something like one solar and a bloody lunar harem more or less.<br /> That's my reasoning i hope i make sense...</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really. The new arrangement means that bonds are forged from past life relationships between special pairs, rather than those relationships being forced on every pair by the bond. That, plus being an option, makes them <i>more significant</i> when they do happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-26-2015, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T06:23:51-07:00","id":457976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457962#post457962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if there are 300 Solars and 400 Lunars, maybe all the Solars have mates but the Lunars don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>300 Solars + 100 Sidereal = 400 Lunars<br /> <br /> Maybe the Lunars were split during the Usurpation when some Lunars joined their Sidereal spouses and others fought with their Solar spouses and others simply ran away. Maybe today there are several dozen Lunars who have joined the Bronze Faction in Yu-Shan acting as partners to their spouses, as well as spies, assassins and stalking horses against other Lunars. <br /> <br /> Or, more likely, some Lunars resonated with some Solars, and others didn't, and every Solar didn't have a Lunar mate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T06:36:23-07:00","id":458001,"title":"","content":"Luuuunaaarr threeeeeeeead!<br /> <br /> *shakes fist at sky*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://wondermark.com/c/2007-05-22-302moon.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-26-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T09:23:46-07:00","id":458105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457952#post457952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resisting Meerkat Steals the Spotlight, though - balancing correct portrayal of Dragon-Blooded conflict with Solars and Lunars is tricky. You don't want to paint the Dragon-Blooded as irresistible foes, almost as powerful and with many times the numbers and resources as Solar or Lunar PCs, because that just leads to dead PCs. Conversely, if they can't offer a threat at all, what's the point? Tricky, artful balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may also help for the combat system to offer the greater nuance that I expect it to offer. To my understanding, strategic and tactical decision-making plays a big role in the outcome of a fight. A Solar in her area of expertise is at a big advantage, but it's not an insurmountable one. A Solar warrior who consistently zigs where she should zag against a Dragonblooded warrior of comparable experience who hits all the right notes should generally fall to the Terrestrial. Likewise, even a much better equipped, experienced, and supported Wyld Hunt can be defeated by a smaller number of Solars if they play smart and make better use of the tactical assets they do have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457857#post457857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess writing narrow escapes, conflict avoidance, and guerilla tacticts are lost arts to some authors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of Avatar: the Last Airbender, and just how many of those the Gaang ran into. Hell, there was that 1e fiction piece in Chiaroscuro that did somewhat similar. More of that sort of thing, please.<br /> <br /> Hm, random thought: everyone knows at least a couple tabletop gamers who just will not ever even consider a fight ending in any manner other than the death of one or all parties, no matter how much one emphasizes some potentially better options. I wonder if there's a tendency for fiction in tabletop games to reflect that more than it should?<br /> <hr /><br /> I'll at least ensconce my contribution to the derail in spoiler tags. ^_^o I don't suppose everyone else jabbering about Lunars would be keen on doing likewise? Provided, like me, you lack the willpower to stop or make a new thread?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457976#post457976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">300 Solars + 100 Sidereal = 400 Lunars<br /> <br /> Maybe the Lunars were split during the Usurpation when some Lunars joined their Sidereal spouses and others fought with their Solar spouses and others simply ran away. Maybe today there are several dozen Lunars who have joined the Bronze Faction in Yu-Shan acting as partners to their spouses, as well as spies, assassins and stalking horses against other Lunars.<br /> <br /> Or, more likely, some Lunars resonated with some Solars, and others didn't, and every Solar didn't have a Lunar mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember: not <i>exactly</i> 400, but <i>around</i> 400. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457970#post457970\">Greyman's post</a> above yours summarizes my understanding of the situation. Strong bonds across reincarnation are things that span all reincarnating Exalted and result from strong connections that prior incarnations forged, not something compelled by a deity. No small number of Celestial Exalted (and reincarnating Exigents, etc.) probably had no connection at all.<br /> <br /> Per other dev remarks, Lunars were sufficiently associated with Solars during the First Age that the Sidereals keeping them around just wasn't an option. This is not to say that this had to be without exception (though &quot;several dozen&quot; would feel like a stretch), and a particularly intense connection between a Lunar and a Sidereal or Sidereals (and likely with weaker ties to a Solar/Solars) would seem a strong factor toward that. It doesn't sound like it would be enough for several dozen to be palling around in Yu-Shan; that'd feel like a pretty big thing for the devs to be playing close to the vest, given what else they've been saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the political juxtaposition of the Lunars to everything else at the fall of the First Age, and the assertion that they should be a faction as varied as the Sidereals. This view distances them from the fallen Solar throne and has several boring consequences, starting with their further diminished relevance and continuing on to them being more like Sidereals and less like a unique actor.<br /> <br /> This sort of logic overlooks just how deeply the Lunars were entrenched in the political and social rule of the old Realm, and how inextricably they were connected to Solar rule. Lunars were the hands, eyes, and mouths of the Solars. They could even wear their faces! If the usurpers considered everything the Solars touched to have been tainted, Lunars would be at the top of the list. And through their power and influence, and their very nature, they represented a massive personal threat to the Sidereal Exalted, and always had\u2014the Lunars were always much, much closer to the throne than the Sidereals were.<br /> <br /> You could no more ignore the Lunars than Westeros could ignore Daenerys.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T10:20:11-07:00","id":458140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=457879#post457879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in <i>A Day Dark as Night</i>, Risa puts up a decent fight against Harmonious Jade.<br /> <br /> In <i>In Northern Twilight</i> the circle faced by newly exalted Swan and Arianna were quite disfunctional, and apparently set up to fall by Gold Faction manipulation, as was Magistrate Gerik when challenged Swan later.<br /> <br /> The 'false' wild hunt Swan faced in <i>A Shadow Over Heavens Eye</i> was a bit more of a challenge, but it was also established to be less than optimal.<br /> <br /> However, the hunt lead by Holok against young Yushuv in <i>Chosen of the Sun</i> had no such excuses. They were totally Worfed to show how bad-arsed Yushuv had become.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why I avoided terms such as &quot;all fiction&quot; and &quot;always suck&quot; and the like. There are a few examples of them being done right.<br /> <br /> Also, I actually loved Risa. She was pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T11:54:11-07:00","id":458219,"title":"","content":"I wish Risa wasn't characterised as the submissive Dragon-Blooded ideal in Caste Book Dawn/Scroll of Exalts.<br /> I've heard before that she's better in the novels but I've never read them due to a combination of complaints about their overall quality and the fact I prefer to read entire novels in deadtree format.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T14:39:38-07:00","id":458354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458105#post458105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may also help for the combat system to offer the greater nuance that I expect it to offer. To my understanding, strategic and tactical decision-making plays a big role in the outcome of a fight. A Solar in her area of expertise is at a big advantage, but it's not an insurmountable one. A Solar warrior who consistently zigs where she should zag against a Dragonblooded warrior of comparable experience who hits all the right notes should generally fall to the Terrestrial. Likewise, even a much better equipped, experienced, and supported Wyld Hunt can be defeated by a smaller number of Solars if they play smart and make better use of the tactical assets they do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing ever being truly guaranteed is a huge positive for me.<br /> <br /> Yes, I like my characters to be successful, but if the system is set up so that I can never be truly challenged in my area of expertise, that gets really boring to play really fast. If the DB plays smarter than me because I'm hopped up on Solar hubris and ends up winning, I deserve what I get!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:02:33-07:00","id":458368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458219#post458219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Risa wasn't characterised as the submissive Dragon-Blooded ideal in Caste Book Dawn/Scroll of Exalts.<br /> I've heard before that she's better in the novels but I've never read them due to a combination of complaints about their overall quality and the fact I prefer to read entire novels in deadtree format.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. That lazy arsed motivation they gave her. Basically just &quot;do whatever Dace wants no questions asked&quot;. Because that's <i>such</i> an excellent example to give of Allie motivation to offer. (sarc)<br /> <br /> In the novelettes at least she's portrayed as a loyal and steadfast lieutenant (and a competent one), <i>but</i> who doesn't exactly agree with the wisdom of every decision Dace makes and <i>isn't shy</i> about telling him so to his face during briefings. She doesn't disobey or undermine his authority in the field, but submissive she isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T17:41:26-07:00","id":458508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458368#post458368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. That lazy arsed motivation they gave her. Basically just &amp;quot;do whatever Dace wants no questions asked&amp;quot;. Because that's <i>such</i> an excellent example to give of Allie motivation to offer. (sarc)<br /> <br /> In the novelettes at least she's portrayed as a loyal and steadfast lieutenant (and a competent one), <i>but</i> who doesn't exactly agree with the wisdom of every decision Dace makes and <i>isn't shy</i> about telling him so to his face during briefings. She doesn't disobey or undermine his authority in the field, but submissive she isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they also do a better job of explaining how Dace's big sexy mug got her to do a 180 from dreaming about hunting anathema since she was a little girl to being the dog-loyal second in command that she is now? True her commander got decapitated before he could move, but from the perspective of a realm raised Dynast you'd think the only two responses to that are tactical retreat or heroic last stand. <br /> <br /> I get her thing is being headstrong and independent, but what if some abyssal chopped Dace's head off? Would she flip over to being all in it for the oblivion? Tell me they showed her having doubts about the anathema at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T17:59:49-07:00","id":458517,"title":"","content":"Risa isn't a Dynast raised in the Realm. She was a Lost Egg or Outcaste adopted into House V'neef. I don't have an answer for the rest of that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T18:35:17-07:00","id":458536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458001#post458001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luuuunaaarr threeeeeeeead!<br /> <br /> *shakes fist at sky*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.p