oz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://imgflip.com/i/jdm08\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/jdm08.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T21:40:23-07:00","id":458655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458219#post458219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Risa wasn't characterised as the submissive Dragon-Blooded ideal in Caste Book Dawn/Scroll of Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may, a brief historical reenactment.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Pay's the Thing, or As You Like It&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatis Personae</u><br /> The Castebook of the Dawn: <i>A Gamee Supplemente</i><br /> Young Coik: <i>A youthful coik</i><br /> A Bear: <i>A bear</i><br /> <br /> Setting: A small room in Wisconsin, circa 2001.<br /> <br /> The Castebook of the Dawn: When I'm with him, following his orders and fighting beside him are the most natural things in the world. If he is any example, I believe that my kind instinctively follow the Solars much as young animals naturally obey their mothers.<br /> <br /> Young Coik: Hark! What bedeviled rubbish be this? I find these engravings to be of the most contemtable slander, and thus I castith both scorn and apsiration upon it. <br /> A Bear (<i>approachs</i>): Indeed. I feelith that this be a poor sentiment to establish for a nascent property.<br /> Young Coik: Noith shitith. (<i>looks</i>) Gadzooks! Thou art that ursine devil that hunts me!<br /> A Bear: Indeed. But when thou art right, thou art right.<br /> Young Coik: Why hast thou not taken the moment of mine distraction to slay me?<br /> A Bear: I bear thee no ill will. Thy father the king wishes thee slain; I merely fulfill my obligation.<br /> Young Coik: Was that a pune?<br /> A Bear: Comeith again?<br /> Young Coik: A pune, or play on words.<br /> A Bear: I know not of what thou speakith. However, I must now --<br /> Young Coik: Lookith! It is the aurora borelious!<br /> A Bear: Here?!?<br /> Young Coik: (<i>throws The Castebook of the Dawn at A Bear</i><br /> A Bear: Arrggh! Thou devil!<br /> Young Coik: Avaunt! (<i>Exit, pursued by bear</i>)<br /> <br /> ~fin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T00:07:24-07:00","id":458722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458508#post458508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they also do a better job of explaining how Dace's big sexy mug got her to do a 180 from dreaming about hunting anathema since she was a little girl to being the dog-loyal second in command that she is now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No ... they completely glossed over it.<br /> <br /> Risa's brief intro in <i>Day Dark as Night</i> just mentioned that she'd set out into the Threshold to mature and <i>eventually</i> joined Dace's mercenary company in Nexus because <i>somewhere</i> a long the way she'd come to know and respect him as a commander despite his being Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T00:22:49-07:00","id":458727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458722#post458722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No ... they completely glossed over it.<br /> <br /> Risa's brief intro in <i>Day Dark as Night</i> just mentioned that she'd set out into the Threshold to mature and <i>eventually</i> joined Dace's mercenary company in Nexus because <i>somewhere</i> a long the way she'd come to know and respect him as a commander despite his being Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least I buy that could happen, even if it's glossed over. I know both we and the author know that Dace is an awesome dude, but Risa has spent most of her life, even the parts where she wasn't living in the Realm, having it drilled into her that anathema are some of the worst kind of monsters imaginable, she was a real true believer in the faith. Over a couple of months though I'd say that a real hero like Dace could change her mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T00:27:50-07:00","id":458728,"title":"","content":"It should also be borne in mind that the Immaculate Order stresses that Anathema love to pretend to be real heroes, so if you meet an Anathema who seems like he's honest, true, and good, well that's just part of his cunning plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T01:35:12-07:00","id":458748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458728#post458728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should also be borne in mind that the Immaculate Order stresses that Anathema love to pretend to be real heroes, so if you meet an Anathema who seems like he's honest, true, and good, well that's just part of his cunning plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I cannot trust your words. Hell, maybe you've even told yourself that enough that you honestly believe it now. But no matter what your intentions, I cannot let you go. You may not look like a monster, but if I let you go you will bring ruin on this realm. You may not want to, but you will become a monster. I am sorry.&quot; -Immaculate Monk #234 vs Solar Hero #57<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T02:38:43-07:00","id":458768,"title":"","content":"I don't mind submissive characters. I even like well written stories with D/s themes, regerdless if they are platonic or erotic. But then, I like to read what happens in at least one of the participants mind during the journey. So a story where Risa goes from believing in the Immaculate Faith, to becoming loyal to Dace, sounds like it could be a story I want to read; if it has her struggling with her thougths and feelings.<br /> <br /> Now, I would find DB = submissive, Solar=Dominant as a general rule equally boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T13:13:03-07:00","id":459319,"title":"","content":"I remember a mixed game I was in once. Two Solars, a Lunar and me, the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> During the course of the adventure, we had gotten embroiled in a war. We were all pretty badass warriors, though naturally the Celestials were a fraction bit better than I was. Still, we held our own most of the time. However, I was the only one with any War, accompanied by War Charms. So during that moment, they all had to look up to me and follow my orders. It was a wonderful feeling, being more knowledgeable and powerful than the accompanying Celestial Exalts in that instance. <br /> <br /> Of course, most of the time that I play a Dragon-Blood, my social skills are generally top-notch, and the other players kind of look to my character as the leader of the group. And a Dragon-Blooded leading a Circle of Celestials tickles my fancy in a very good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T14:38:56-07:00","id":459380,"title":"","content":"Which is a good justification in-setting for telling the Celestials that to give up the notion that Dragon-Blooded should &quot;naturally&quot; be their servants. The trouble or course comes anyway, when they use social charms, fate-manipulation, memory-alteration, and/or threats to MAKE the DBs serve them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T14:50:47-07:00","id":459404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=459380#post459380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a good justification in-setting for telling the Celestials that to give up the notion that Dragon-Blooded should &quot;naturally&quot; be their servants. The trouble or course comes anyway, when they use social charms, fate-manipulation, memory-alteration, and/or threats to MAKE the DBs serve them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone is using that kind of thing on other <i>players </i>to compel their actions then the OOC gaming environment is already toxically disrespectful.<br /> <br /> Also that notion that DBs should serve them cannot reasonably arise IC for a long time, depending on what ancient lore has been unearthed. It would be pretty OOC-driven. And that's shitty metagaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-27-2015, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T19:02:08-07:00","id":459587,"title":"","content":"I've seen it arise through a combination of gross metagaming and super-high past lives shenanigans.<br /> <br /> When the solar in question actually gets around to voicing that opinion to the two Dragon-Bloods that are his only remaining friends, it isn't going to be pretty.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, that sounds like a great idea! I think the last time someone tried it, the Dragons were so enamored of the idea that they rose up and murdered everyone, and kept on murdering them for centuries so it'd never happen again! I love this plan! I'm excited to be a part of it!&quot;<br /> &quot;Really? It seems like you'd take this a lot worse th-*hurk*&quot;<br /> &quot;No. *stab*&quot;<br /> <br /> On topic, chapter fiction or the like seems like exactly the sort of time you might want to see Solars getting murdered, on account of it's chapter fiction so there are no &quot;protagonists&quot; and it doesn't have to involve anybody &quot;recurring&quot; or &quot;canonical&quot; that should rightly survive to build a story around. I'd actually really like to see a Solar getting taken down hard that isn't pathetic (that kid) or at the hands of one of his buddies (that Kidale). You know, heroic spirit, back to the wall, epic showdown, LOSE.<br /> <br /> Cultivate the idea that you know, that actually happens sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-27-2015, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:14:25-07:00","id":460744,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, im going to use this thread as a starting point for another very aggravating point that needs to die in a fire, but is tangentially related.<br /> <br /> In other threads, I've seen for a long time now about the 'lesser effects' and, as others have said, 'lolnope' effects that Dragon-Blooded magic is powerless against. And a lot of the time, its phrased something like &quot;Mortals and Dragonbloods are powerless to stop X effect, celestials have an easier time of it blah blah blah&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are weaker than the Celestial Exalted. The Dragon-Blooded are Exalted. Why are they getting lumped in with regular mortals? This is bullshit. The line should not be a (Mortal+Terrestrial / Celestial) divide. It should <i>instead</i> be a (mortal / Terrestrial+Celestial). Making them every bit as weak to effects as a regular mortal furthers the idea that DBs are pointless extras when beside a Celestial.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand that Celestial may have a greater resistance to, or more power over, certain effects. But the way its presented currently is just bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:36:09-07:00","id":460762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=460744#post460744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighty, im going to use this thread as a starting point for another very aggravating point that needs to die in a fire, but is tangentially related.<br /> <br /> In other threads, I've seen for a long time now about the 'lesser effects' and, as others have said, 'lolnope' effects that Dragon-Blooded magic is powerless against. And a lot of the time, its phrased something like &amp;quot;Mortals and Dragonbloods are powerless to stop X effect, celestials have an easier time of it blah blah blah&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are weaker than the Celestial Exalted. The Dragon-Blooded are Exalted. Why are they getting lumped in with regular mortals? This is bullshit. The line should not be a (Mortal+Terrestrial / Celestial) divide. It should <i>instead</i> be a (mortal / Terrestrial+Celestial). Making them every bit as weak to effects as a regular mortal furthers the idea that DBs are pointless extras when beside a Celestial.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand that Celestial may have a greater resistance to, or more power over, certain effects. But the way its presented currently is just bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mostly a weak way of explaining away why DBs haven't done X thing in the setting. Like why they couldn't fight the contagion or why they didn't raid your first age tomb or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:00:31-07:00","id":462624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=459587#post459587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, heroic spirit, back to the wall, epic showdown, LOSE.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this happens <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">to a Night Caste in the 6 novel series. I can't remember which book, though.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:12:46-07:00","id":462734,"title":"","content":"This reminds me a lot of the discussion that was had on &quot;what antagonists should we see in third edition&quot;. I once again despair that there seem to be a large group of posters who believe that Solar exalts should be more like starting vampire characters than they should be the natural saviours or destroyers of creation.<br /> <br /> Apparently its ok for solars to beat up an experienced dragon blood, maybe, after long character arcs and much xp expenditure. Well, lovely as that is, Dragon Blooded are not Solars, should not be considered on the solar scale and their ability to fight is down to their numbers, equipment and occasionally, their abilities.<br /> <br /> Solars are meant to be world shaking and they are meant to be world shaking, be it socially or physically, from day one and hour one. Otherwise, what is the point? Are we really saying that the player party should cower from the threat of the Wyld hunt being called down upon them until they are all in warstriders and owning half of creation? Should a party of dragon blooded be enough to send the players running to the hills to come up with some complex plan to maybe challenge them?<br /> <br /> Call me old fashioned, but I feel Exalted was meant to break the mold of &quot;neonate vampire sucks&quot; and the world should not be populated with things that make starting solar characters seem less awesome than they are. If that was the case, then there would be no solars and Dragon Blooded would be the only exalted type in the game. The alternative is that the dragon blooded simply execute all the solars and we are all left wondering what everyone was getting so worried about in their return.<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded are noble underdogs whose time in the setting has passed. The return of the solars should not simply be a tactical concern for them, it should be the apocalypse, the turning of a new age where their empire is utterly destroyed and a new world, for better or worse, is put in its place. It is not &quot;business as normal&quot; for the terrestrials, its a moment of abject terror where their usual might is suddenly made obsolete and they are kicked around in the same way they kick around mortals, in a tremendous reversal of fortunes.<br /> <br /> Again, if this is not so, then what is the point in playing solars, or in the awesome nature of their glorious and terrifying en-mass return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","name":"Silvercat18","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4104_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:50:07-07:00","id":462759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me a lot of the discussion that was had on &quot;what antagonists should we see in third edition&quot;. I once again despair that there seem to be a large group of posters who believe that Solar exalts should be more like starting vampire characters than they should be the natural saviours or destroyers of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's that 99% of the setting shouldn't automatically not matter to Solars except in terms of &quot;how easily can I murder them or make them my enslaved puppet.&quot; That was the state of affairs in 2e with mortals. It was shitty to make that the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently its ok for solars to beat up an experienced dragon blood, maybe, after long character arcs and much xp expenditure. Well, lovely as that is, Dragon Blooded are not Solars, should not be considered on the solar scale and their ability to fight is down to their numbers, equipment and occasionally, their abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically speaking, it's complete Worfing if a powerful and experienced DB gets punked by a brand-new Solar. A game line should not be in the habit of Worfing <i>other playable splats</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are meant to be world shaking and they are meant to be world shaking, be it socially or physically, from day one and hour one. Otherwise, what is the point? Are we really saying that the player party should cower from the threat of the Wyld hunt being called down upon them until they are all in warstriders and owning half of creation? Should a party of dragon blooded be enough to send the players running to the hills to come up with some complex plan to maybe challenge them?</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of hyperbole barely merits response, but I'll go ahead.<br /> <br /> DBs have numbers and infrastructure and institutional experience. Letting a Solar trump all that just because they're a Solar means &quot;nothing matters except that your anima is gold.&quot; That's a bad message and it makes for boring games, frankly, when the only enemy the ST can reasonably challenge a Solar with is a bunch of DBs or another Celestial.<br /> <br /> And if the Wyld Hunt has no teeth, then the setting is totally inconsistent. And that also sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me old fashioned, but I feel Exalted was meant to break the mold of &quot;neonate vampire sucks&quot; and the world should not be populated with things that make starting solar characters seem less awesome than they are. If that was the case, then there would be no solars and Dragon Blooded would be the only exalted type in the game. The alternative is that the dragon blooded simply execute all the solars and we are all left wondering what everyone was getting so worried about in their return.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think the goal for 3e is to devolve to &quot;neonate vampire suckage,&quot; I'd kindly ask you to provide a cite to the devs saying that's their intent. I seriously doubt you can cite anything that could reasonably interpreted in that manner. <br /> <br /> Solars stand tall and shake the heavens - that does not mean than obviating 99% of the setting in the face of a chargen Solar is good design. It simply is not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Blooded are noble underdogs whose time in the setting has passed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolute bullshit. It might be valid if DBs were NPC-only. But they're not. So no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The return of the solars should not simply be a tactical concern for them, it should be the apocalypse, the turning of a new age where their empire is utterly destroyed and a new world, for better or worse, is put in its place. It is not &quot;business as normal&quot; for the terrestrials, its a moment of abject terror where their usual might is suddenly made obsolete and they are kicked around in the same way they kick around mortals, in a tremendous reversal of fortunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it isn't? You're making an awful lot of unfounded assumptions. <br /> <br /> And for the return of the Solars to inherently topple the Realm, without a fight...sorry, that's awful and shouldn't happen at all. 10,000 aren't obsolete just because 300 Solars come back. Those Solars should really be careful not to wake the dragon while it's chewing on its own tail, or secretly back a faction they think they can exploit. If 300 Solars walked toward the Realm with intent to lay it low, I guarantee they'd all die. So would a bunch of DB, though, but nothing would unify the Realm away from its civil war squabbles like an existential threat such as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T16:33:59-07:00","id":462799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462759#post462759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practically speaking, it's complete Worfing if a powerful and experienced DB gets punked by a brand-new Solar. A game line should not be in the habit of Worfing <i>other playable splats</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but even if it wasn't a playable splat it would suck, if it just got switched over to fey who were always showing up in random places to get the crap kicked out of them it'd suck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462759#post462759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs have numbers and infrastructure and institutional experience. Letting a Solar trump all that just because they're a Solar means &quot;nothing matters except that your anima is gold.&quot; That's a bad message and it makes for boring games, frankly, when the only enemy the ST can reasonably challenge a Solar with is a bunch of DBs or another Celestial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a bunch of DBs in most stories are not going to be going after a single Solar, the party is made up of Solars. A few DBs against a whole party of 5 Solars isn't as big a deal. Saying that 5 DBs hunting down one Solar is a suicide mission takes it a little too far.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462759#post462759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is absolute bullshit. It might be valid if DBs were NPC-only. But they're not. So no.<br /> <br /> And for the return of the Solars to inherently topple the Realm, without a fight...sorry, that's awful and shouldn't happen at all. 10,000 aren't obsolete just because 300 Solars come back. Those Solars should really be careful not to wake the dragon while it's chewing on its own tail, or secretly back a faction they think they can exploit. If 300 Solars walked toward the Realm with intent to lay it low, I guarantee they'd all die. So would a bunch of DB, though, but nothing would unify the Realm away from its civil war squabbles like an existential threat such as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>ehhh I think if all 150 Solars charged the Blessed Isle the Realm would be toppled in days at the most. Part of what makes Solars not instantly winning everything is that they're by far the most fractured splat in the whole of Creation. The Realm is seriously on the decline and can't even do the kind of Hunts that they used to do when there were little more than a dozen Solar exaltations floating around. Not to mention the Abyssals and Infernals with backing.<br /> <br /> That being said some of the fiction in second edition gave the impression that if you kicked down a pompus satrap in the middle of the city, only to have a dozen terrestrial anima banners ignite around you as you realize you've just sprung the trap...that the correct response is to laugh and draw your daiklave. Which unless you exploited the scenelong charms wasn't even mechanically a good idea because you'd get your fucking ass kicked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:23:40-07:00","id":462874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462799#post462799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ehhh I think if all 150 Solars charged the Blessed Isle the Realm would be toppled in days at the most. Part of what makes Solars not instantly winning everything is that they're by far the most fractured splat in the whole of Creation. The Realm is seriously on the decline and can't even do the kind of Hunts that they used to do when there were little more than a dozen Solar exaltations floating around. Not to mention the Abyssals and Infernals with backing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you with everything except this, where I have to side with Zelbinnean.<br /> <br /> Just 150 Solars trying to take out the realm... Solars are good, but I highly doubt they could stand up to the artillery that the Realm can bring to bear against them. Not to mention, such a large gathering of Solars is sure to bring the attention of heaven, which could alert the Realm, and let them prepare. Of course, this is assuming just all the solars got up and started running full speed to the blessed isle with a single minded focus.<br /> <br /> Now, a big part of being a solar is the resources they can bring to bear. And if they used those.. .building their armies, calling on ancient favors, making deals and forcing cooperation from other groups, then all of them doing that towards the single goal of taking down the Realm...yeah, they're going to probably succeed. Especially if they, say, infiltrate heaven, re-learn the secrets to the Realm Defense Grid and smuggle a small group of themselves in there.<br /> <br /> But the Realm is still strong. Its on the decline, but in the face of such an adversary, and if they banded together again, they would be a foe every bit as powerful as nearly anything that could be thrown at them. The might of 10,000+ dragons is no small thing, and even Solars can't be certain of victory when faced with another Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:36:41-07:00","id":462882,"title":"","content":"The hard balance point is how to make the Realm a credible threat without making it impossible to overcome. Or making it possible for Solars to not be completely dead from challenging the Wyld Hunt without also making it a paper tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:44:37-07:00","id":462890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ehhh I think if all 150 Solars charged the Blessed Isle the Realm would be toppled in days at the most. Part of what makes Solars not instantly winning everything is that they're by far the most fractured splat in the whole of Creation. The Realm is seriously on the decline and can't even do the kind of Hunts that they used to do when there were little more than a dozen Solar exaltations floating around. Not to mention the Abyssals and Infernals with backing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they would. I mean, in 10 or 20 years, yeah, but at the moment the average Solar has been exalted for about 2 years, they're little more than starting characters. Whereas the average DB has been exalted for 50 or so years.<br /> Solars are the Shonen protagonists. They have incredible potential, and by the end of the story they'll be more powerful than anyone else, but right now they lack the experience to crush empires underfoot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:46:30-07:00","id":462891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462734#post462734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>If an experienced Dragon-Blooded will be killed 100% of the time by a newborn Solar, then why make the Dragon-Blooded playable at all? The Solars are good, and as you say, world-shaking. They are excellence and perfection, but I feel what they are most of all is potential.<br /> <br /> The potential of what a Solar can do is staggering. But that lies in gaining experience, surviving in a world that half the people want you dead, and learning. And that potential never lessens. Even once they've reached mastery of something, there's still so much more they can do.<br /> <br /> That said, this is only slightly less true for the other Exalted. Being Chosen is being gifted with the power to do limitless wonders. Its harder for some to express it, but its still there. Personally, i feel like Exaltation is giving a character the <b>PC</b> <b>Character</b> tag, even if they aren't controlled by a player. It means they're able to do miraculous and outstanding things, above the norm. Every single exalt you come across should feel like this, a potential friend or party member, a lover or an extremely dangerous foe. The feeling you get when you might kill another players character is the feeling you should feel should you choose that you need to kill an Exalt, because you will be trying to destroy something blessed by gods and sacred, whether they're a douche or not.<br /> <br /> So every instance of a Wyld Hunt should be a story as amazing as if both sides were controlled by players. Neither side should be offing the other casually. Newborn Solars aren't going to be laying waste to an entire Wyld Hunt and then strutting off to f*ck b*tch*s, and the Dragon-Blooded aren't likely to off the Solar in a single blow and then snort cocaine off his dead body.<br /> <br /> A Terrestrial vs a Solar, the odds are in the Solar's favor. But it should never be a completely 100% outcome, especially between equally experienced characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:10:19-07:00","id":462942,"title":"","content":"Especially because a combat where you 100% know who will win is extremely boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:20:11-07:00","id":463077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462799#post462799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ehhh I think if all 150 Solars charged the Blessed Isle the Realm would be toppled in days at the most. Part of what makes Solars not instantly winning everything is that they're by far the most fractured splat in the whole of Creation. The Realm is seriously on the decline and can't even do the kind of Hunts that they used to do when there were little more than a dozen Solar exaltations floating around. Not to mention the Abyssals and Infernals with backing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ran it with 2E game mechanics, yes. By the fluff? Helllllll no. Keep in mind that at the height of their power the large majority of the First Age Solar Exalted were killed by a small fraction of the Dragon-Blooded at a party. Attacking the Isle in force would be beyond idiotic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:31:18-07:00","id":463120,"title":"","content":"It's better to have new players be proud of the fact that they defeated the dreaded Wyld Hunt than to have the PCs be fatally blindsided by Dragon-Blooded competence.<br /> <br /> I've joked before now that the Udon Comic captures the experience of 2e mechanical problems rather well 4/5 Dragon-Blooded get taken out the fight without much of a fuss, the 5th uses a bullshit charm the players hadn't prepared for causing the Dawn to kill the Eclipse causing their players to become disatisified and leave resulting in the game disintegrating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:58:50-07:00","id":463214,"title":"","content":"Neither the setting nor the mechanics were written with the expectation that 100% of all Solars shake Creation down to its foundation on day 1 of their Exaltation. For one thing, Solars have been Exalting for thousands of years, and the vast majority of the ones that did so during the times of the Shogunate or the Realm ended up with their heads on spikes, perishing in the holy fires of the Dragon-Blooded, overwhelmed by a monster they unwisely called up, knifed in the back by people they thought were friends, et cetera. If the setting had been written the way Silvercat seems to assume, Creation would not be recognizable because the Realm (or indeed, any of the institutions of Creation) would not have been able to stand up to the might of the dozen or so Solars that could shake up the world from day 1.<br /> <br /> They have the potential to shake things up, but it's far from automatic. The Exalted, all of them, are mighty, but they have feet of clay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2015, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T04:40:38-07:00","id":463314,"title":"","content":"Heads on spikes indeed, until the bull of the North stuck a spike on a helmet and said &quot;much better combination, spike on head, not head on spike.&quot; And thus his conquest began.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:17:03-07:00","id":463485,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that you don't get charms right away upon exaltation, you have to learn them over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:44:09-07:00","id":463587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=463485#post463485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that you don't get charms right away upon exaltation, you have to learn them over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make a lot of characters' exaltation stories very odd. Like how Lyta fought her way out of an immaculate monestary and stuff. You could say that the moment of exaltation grants you incredible power for a little while, but then it fades and you have to relearn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:03:23-07:00","id":463596,"title":"","content":"Huh. Yeah that does seem to be the common exaltation narrative, doesn't it? I dunno what to say. It's something I hope 3E clarifies. Even though starting characters probably still default to 0.5-1 year after exaltation, it would be nice to know how it all goes, especially since &quot;heroic mortals who exalt during play&quot; is still a cool game premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:13:12-07:00","id":463631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=463596#post463596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Yeah that does seem to be the common exaltation narrative, doesn't it? I dunno what to say. It's something I hope 3E clarifies. Even though starting characters probably still default to 0.5-1 year after exaltation, it would be nice to know how it all goes, especially since &amp;quot;heroic mortals who exalt during play&amp;quot; is still a cool game premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it needs written clarification. Do what you think is cool for your game, whether that means that newly-Exalted people basically instantly develop the native Charms associated with their strengths and personalities (very possible with native Charms being expressions of existing skill and not Techniques!) or starting just with Excellencies and needing some time to figure out how to unleash the rest of their free starting allotment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:22:07-07:00","id":463721,"title":"","content":"It's never been officially stated for what the mechanics at the moment of Exaltation are, and I doubt we'll ever see those.<br /> <br /> In my games (it's come up a few times in games where the players Exalt during the course of the story), for the scene in which he Exalts, the character's Essence is treated as if it were 5, and he can essentially use every Charm for which he meets the Ability/Attribute requirements. This means, for that one scene, an Exalt is one terrifying motherfucker. Then, every scene after that, the character's Essence lowers by 1 until it reaches 2, at which point the character loses all but a handful of Charms and must begin learning Charms and raising Essence as normal.<br /> <br /> This will probably give the character the opportunity to survive or deal with whatever danger he may have been in at the moment of Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:26:22-07:00","id":464182,"title":"","content":"My games have done both. Sometimes, they get a powerboost that is dealt with totally without mechanics. They're just basically badass against whatever was threatening them.<br /> <br /> Other times, the character Exalts, and while he doesn't know that he has all those Charms, by doing his best, they automatically activate with the attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T22:19:21-07:00","id":464274,"title":"","content":"Actually I think at some point the errata document had rules, of a sort, for what happens during the scene of an <i>Abyssal</i> Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T22:21:55-07:00","id":464276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=462891#post462891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Terrestrial vs a Solar, the odds are in the Solar's favor. But it should never be a completely 100% outcome, especially between equally experienced characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this silly hope that perhaps clever application of charms, preparation and wild, unexpected tactics ought to allow a Dragon Blood to negate a dumb Solar's raw power advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T23:41:53-07:00","id":464345,"title":"","content":"I think, at the end of the day in a white room duel, a battle between a Dawn and a Terrestrial with similar builds and experience is almost always going to end with the Dawn winning. <br /> <br /> But, if a Water Aspect can pull the Dawn into a fight in the middle of a lake, or a Fire Aspect can fight in the middle of a massive burning building, or the Terrestrial can fly around and shoot the Dawn who only has melee charms and can't respond, the environmental factors might give them a huge or even insurmountable advantage. And of course you always have things like poisoning the Dawn's food or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Dawn might have Charms of effects that allow them to be immune or resistant (maybe the Dawn can fly or can shoot energy beams, or can breath underwater or resist fire). <br /> <br /> Ultimately a combat-focused Solar will generally have an easier time killing a combat-focused Terrestrial than the Terrestrial killing the Solar. Ultimately that's just the nature of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T23:48:57-07:00","id":464349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=464276#post464276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this silly hope that perhaps clever application of charms, preparation and wild, unexpected tactics ought to allow a Dragon Blood to negate a dumb Solar's raw power advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not silly. That's very likely.<br /> <br /> Dumb fighters tend to be great at dying. Even better if they are just dumb individuals in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 04-01-2015, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:26:33-07:00","id":464386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=464345#post464345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, at the end of the day in a white room duel, a battle between a Dawn and a Terrestrial with similar builds and experience is almost always going to end with the Dawn winning.<br /> <br /> But, if a Water Aspect can pull the Dawn into a fight in the middle of a lake, or a Fire Aspect can fight in the middle of a massive burning building, or the Terrestrial can fly around and shoot the Dawn who only has melee charms and can't respond, the environmental factors might give them a huge or even insurmountable advantage. And of course you always have things like poisoning the Dawn's food or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Dawn might have Charms of effects that allow them to be immune or resistant (maybe the Dawn can fly or can shoot energy beams, or can breath underwater or resist fire).<br /> <br /> Ultimately a combat-focused Solar will generally have an easier time killing a combat-focused Terrestrial than the Terrestrial killing the Solar. Ultimately that's just the nature of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the most ardent of Terrestrial apologists, I don't think that has ever really been the main gripe against Solar's. From what I can tell, the gripe has always been that Solars have options and builds that are more powerful to a degree that they can kill any number of Terrestrials without having a chance at failure. Or that there is no amount of lateral thinking, low cunning, preparation, or creative tactics which can allow a Terrestrial to usurp the advantage that even a dumb Solar has. But then, 2e was a dark age for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:29:43-07:00","id":464387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=464386#post464386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from the most ardent of Terrestrial apologists, I don't think that has ever really been the main gripe against Solar's. From what I can tell, the gripe has always been that Solars have options and builds that are more powerful to a degree that they can kill any number of Terrestrials without having a chance at failure. Or that there is no amount of lateral thinking, low cunning, preparation, or creative tactics which can allow a Terrestrial to usurp the advantage that even a dumb Solar has. But then, 2e was a dark age for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah preserving that whole tier thing where Solars had to be the most powerful exalts caused a few problems. Well that and the problems that melting dice pools brought to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:42:32-07:00","id":464394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=463120#post463120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's better to have new players be proud of the fact that they defeated the dreaded Wyld Hunt than to have the PCs be fatally blindsided by Dragon-Blooded competence.<br /> <br /> I've joked before now that the Udon Comic captures the experience of 2e mechanical problems rather well 4/5 Dragon-Blooded get taken out the fight without much of a fuss, the 5th uses a bullshit charm the players hadn't prepared for causing the Dawn to kill the Eclipse causing their players to become disatisified and leave resulting in the game disintegrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes I play around with house ruling in a Fate Point system similar to what the WH40K TRPG line has. Something that gives the players an opportunity to burn a finite resource which can only be earned by achieving big things which allows them to survive an otherwise hopeless situation, if only just. In the stuff for that line that I have run, having fate points encouraged players to take some risks, live on the edge, and try some cool and interesting things without the fear that they will immediately gib their character. It wouldn't work for every game or campaign, but I think it would fit with a lot of the more pulpy Exalted campaigns. After all, narrow escapes from certain death have always been a part of mythology and pulp fiction. But IDK, it has always seemed to me like a good way to have your cake and not have it murder your players because they walked into a situation not fully prepared.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=464387#post464387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah preserving that whole tier thing where Solars had to be the most powerful exalts caused a few problems. Well that and the problems that melting dice pools brought to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stuff the devs have been saying about getting tiers out of the game and having a more holistic perspective on strengths and weaknesses have more or less caused me to make audible squees of joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T06:45:09-08:00","id":770695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=458508#post458508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they also do a better job of explaining how Dace's big sexy mug got her to do a 180 from dreaming about hunting anathema since she was a little girl to being the dog-loyal second in command that she is now? True her commander got decapitated before he could move, but from the perspective of a realm raised Dynast you'd think the only two responses to that are tactical retreat or heroic last stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so, somebody recently liked one of my posts in this thread and it got me to re-read some of it....does anyone else feel like the DB story in the core is basically Risa's story except twice as bad? I've already posted how I feel about every single fiction in the corebook, but I'll repeat that I really like the Dawn character in it, and I think it's cool that an older woman is given some aspect of sexuality, because way too often writers seem to feel that after 40 women must lose all interest in sex.<br /> <br /> On the other hand though, she's an elder magistrate, someone who's supposed to not only be personally powerful but also with strong convictions. You don't pick somebody to be judge, jury and executioner if a wink and a hand full of jade will get them to do whatever you want. Sadly she gets her ass resoundingly handed to her, and right after she agrees to serve this sexy, sexy Dawn caste and join his demon-conquest of her homeland.<br /> <br /> Again, I personally know that One Million Perfect Petals is a good dude. Strong, merciful, charismatic, and empowered by the sun to do right in Creation. It's just that this is the DB story and it doesn't make them out to be good antagonists, or good protagonists. As a protagonist character in the story she gets her ass beat by somebody who outclasses her, and then turns traitor to her home, her nation and her family. Because, obviously if there's one thing a DB would stab in the back, it's their family. But she doesn't work as a threatening antagonist either because she seems kind of fickle and weak. The Lunar, Sidereal, Liminal, and Exigent stories all come out feeling cool and powerful. I'm still not so hot on the Abyssal one either, but it's more in the presentation than the assumption that 100 spine chains are not threatening.<br /> <br /> The story even slips in some exposition about how a student at the Spiral Academy exalted and the death toll from her escape was terrible. Not even how she killed 50 people before she was finally brought down, she killed a crap ton of people and then got away somehow. The Spiral Academy is located inside the Imperial City by the way. So this teenager who was going to school to be a bureaucrat, so probably exalted Eclipse or Twilight* caste, smack dab in the middle of the Imperial City, carved a path of destruction to...I presume the docks? And then...sailed...away? I can't even imagine how this went down.<br /> <br /> Is it just me or did the herpin-derpinblooded not get off to as good a start as everyone else when it came to showing that they're getting some sweet fiction this edition?<br /> <br /> *Admittedly this is pure conjecture on my part, who knows, maybe they were a student who had also been training their whole life to be a duelist and exalted dawn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T09:37:35-08:00","id":770796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=463596#post463596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Yeah that does seem to be the common exaltation narrative, doesn't it? I dunno what to say. It's something I hope 3E clarifies. Even though starting characters probably still default to 0.5-1 year after exaltation, it would be nice to know how it all goes, especially since &quot;heroic mortals who exalt during play&quot; is still a cool game premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, turns out this was in fact clarified. The Heroic Mortals sidebar has rules for Exalting mid-game, and the way it works is you get the basic 'Exalt' template goodies like healing and not-bleeding-out and not-dying-of-disease immediately, a Limit Trigger, along with 10 out of your 15 standard Character Generation Charms. Then at the end of the current story you gain another 5 Charms, 2 dots of Willpower, 2 dots each in your Primary and Secondary Attributes, and one dot among your Tertiary Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T12:05:34-08:00","id":770878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=770695#post770695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so, somebody recently liked one of my posts in this thread and it got me to re-read some of it....does anyone else feel like the DB story in the core is basically Risa's story except twice as bad? I've already posted how I feel about every single fiction in the corebook, but I'll repeat that I really like the Dawn character in it, and I think it's cool that an older woman is given some aspect of sexuality, because way too often writers seem to feel that after 40 women must lose all interest in sex.<br /> <br /> On the other hand though, she's an elder magistrate, someone who's supposed to not only be personally powerful but also with strong convictions. You don't pick somebody to be judge, jury and executioner if a wink and a hand full of jade will get them to do whatever you want. Sadly she gets her ass resoundingly handed to her, and right after she agrees to serve this sexy, sexy Dawn caste and join his demon-conquest of her homeland.<br /> <br /> Again, I personally know that One Million Perfect Petals is a good dude. Strong, merciful, charismatic, and empowered by the sun to do right in Creation. It's just that this is the DB story and it doesn't make them out to be good antagonists, or good protagonists. As a protagonist character in the story she gets her ass beat by somebody who outclasses her, and then turns traitor to her home, her nation and her family. Because, obviously if there's one thing a DB would stab in the back, it's their family. But she doesn't work as a threatening antagonist either because she seems kind of fickle and weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with all your points, but how exactly did you get the impression she agreed to serve him, betraying her nation and family in the process, especially with the Realm rotting from within and in need of intervention, in need of her, more than ever?<br /> <br /> The fiction closes off on Petals's proposal and leaves ambiguous where it goes from there but I see no indication that Marani actually took it. In fact, every bit of characterization seems to say her reaction would be the exact opposite, and that it wouldn't be nearly as easy as you make it sound to convince her to do otherwise. The story cuts off at an atmospheric point that leaves the details of what happens next open for us to fill in, but it doesn't particularly suggest that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T13:32:08-08:00","id":770919,"title":"","content":"To me this is missing the problem with V'neef Risa.<br /> <br /> It's not that she's a Dynast who found herself working for a Solar after being defeated by them. It's that in 1e we have her talking with apparent authority on what the position of a Dragon-Blooded is supposed to be and in 2e she's written up as an NPC without her own goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T14:25:04-08:00","id":770952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=770878#post770878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree with all your points, but how exactly did you get the impression she agreed to serve him, betraying her nation and family in the process, especially with the Realm rotting from within and in need of intervention, in need of her, more than ever?<br /> <br /> The fiction closes off on Petals's proposal and leaves ambiguous where it goes from there but I see no indication that Marani actually took it. In fact, every bit of characterization seems to say her reaction would be the exact opposite, and that it wouldn't be nearly as easy as you make it sound to convince her to do otherwise. The story cuts off at an atmospheric point that leaves the details of what happens next open for us to fill in, but it doesn't particularly suggest that interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get that interpretation at all. True it doesnt explicitly give her response but it feels pretty unambiguous to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=770919#post770919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me this is missing the problem with V'neef Risa.<br /> <br /> It's not that she's a Dynast who found herself working for a Solar after being defeated by them. It's that in 1e we have her talking with apparent authority on what the position of a Dragon-Blooded is supposed to be and in 2e she's written up as an NPC without her own goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true, she's definitely not a sock puppet without her own motivation. To me though it feels a bit like getting a sith inquisitor to join the rebellion by beating him up and giving him a sexy wink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T15:57:14-08:00","id":771017,"title":"","content":"To be fair, she was cut off and betrayed first; the system no longer supports her, and the Great Houses are basically hunting her for sport. Second, it looks more like an alliance of convenience than another 2E Risa, &quot;guess it's time to turn into a dot on your character sheet.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T18:46:36-08:00","id":771126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771017#post771017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, she was cut off and betrayed first; the system no longer supports her, and the Great Houses are basically hunting her for sport. Second, it looks more like an alliance of convenience than another 2E Risa, &quot;guess it's time to turn into a dot on your character sheet.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but you have to make a lot of assumptions that are kind of unlikely. This might have been a bit of an ambitious story to tell in a single page. Firstly you have to assume she's not brainwashed by the immaculate faith, because your nation would have to be pretty bad to become a servant of Lucifer in order to bring it down. Or take some serious convincing, which I know being a Solar he can do, but she's like a 175 year old salty magistrate, that can't be easy. It's a hard, but possible, assumption to make considering she references him as Anathema and stuff.<br /> <br /> She'd also have to be pretty vindictive about how bad the Realm got and how she was betrayed. She's not joining up with House Nellens and bringing reform to the Great Houses, or putting her foot down and helping the Immaculate Order restore a semblance of decency to the Dynasty. She's becoming the second-in-command of a Dawn cast Solar to get revenge on the Empire. Captain America in The Winter Soldier got betrayed pretty bad, one of his friends killed, and his country about to crush every freedom and liberty he swore his life to protect, but I still don't see him doing a full 180 and leading a conquering army to the shores of his homeland.<br /> <br /> It's not that it's a bad story to do, but &quot;surprise, Cap is a Nazi now.&quot; isn't something that's easy to do in such a small space. It isn't that she got worfed by getting her ass kicked, I mean the only other two stories with DBs in them have them getting thrashed by Dawn castes too, but they're both great. It's just the seeming lack of conviction from one of the chosen champions of the Scarlett Empress, combined with the unexplained Spiral Academy escape, combined with the lame fight rubs me the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T19:26:12-08:00","id":771143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771126#post771126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the only other two stories with DBs in them have them getting thrashed by Dawn Castes\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Thrashed by Dawn Castes?&quot; I remember one in which an armed, armored Dragon-Blooded and a nearly-naked, injured Dawn Caste (singular) <i>started</i> to duel in a burning building at the <i>end</i> of a chapter fiction, but that's not remotely what I'd call &quot;getting thrashed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-21-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T20:14:36-08:00","id":771171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=770952#post770952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me though it feels a bit like getting a sith inquisitor to join the rebellion by beating him up and giving him a sexy wink.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to struggle to find a story of a character switching sides in the heat of the moment that isn't really contrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:24:15-08:00","id":771207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771143#post771143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Thrashed by Dawn Castes?&quot; I remember one in which an armed, armored Dragon-Blooded and a nearly-naked, injured Dawn Caste (singular) <i>started</i> to duel in a burning building at the <i>end</i> of a chapter fiction, but that's not remotely what I'd call &quot;getting thrashed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well okay that one didn't actually have the fight but it's Volfer's Dawn Caste fiction so I'm pretty sure I know where that's going. The other one doesn't really have a &quot;Thrashing&quot; either, but one unarmed and unarmored Dawn gets surprised attacked by a pair of DBs and a Sidereal decked out in artifacts, also a god kind of, and comes out on top. Which were both awesome, Volfer is a bit of a dick but he's also pretty cool, and the intro fiction is probably the best piece of Exalted fiction I've ever read and it's not even 15 pages long. Also in the intro there was some refreshing back and forth. I was kind of hoping the DB fiction would be more about showcasing the horrible, cold cruelty of Dynastic politics, or a more through-their-eyes view of the Realm crushing a satrapy too wounded to fight back, or even an outcaste DB desperately fighting anything but a Dawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771171#post771171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to struggle to find a story of a character switching sides in the heat of the moment that isn't really contrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's my problem with it exactly, I don't have any context for it so it feels cheap. To me anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:30:32-08:00","id":771212,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think scenes like that need the character in question to have already gone through things that incline them towards it. Perhaps a DB witnessed the Realm doing horrible things previously, or read some books that made her question the accuracy of the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> Of course, it could just be that the Solar's that good at convincing people. But that doesn't make DBs feel powerful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:57:20-08:00","id":771221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771212#post771212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think scenes like that need the character in question to have already gone through things that incline them towards it. Perhaps a DB witnessed the Realm doing horrible things previously\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the target of an attempted murder isn't horrible, doesn't incline you to maybe revise your position on backing the guys trying to kill you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:15:39-08:00","id":771232,"title":"","content":"Wait, which scene are we talking about? I'll go re-read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:23:27-08:00","id":771234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771221#post771221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the target of an attempted murder isn't horrible, doesn't incline you to maybe revise your position on backing the guys trying to kill you?</div> </div> </div> </div>When the guys trying to kill me are planning on taking an army to my homeland, burn it to the ground and kill it's people...no, not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771232#post771232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, which scene are we talking about? I'll go re-read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 180 of the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:18:04-08:00","id":771288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=770695#post770695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or did the herpin-derpinblooded not get off to as good a start as everyone else when it came to showing that they're getting some sweet fiction this edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>That piece of fiction didn't resonate with me either, I think it didn't know whose story it was telling. It could have been the Solar's story just told from the perspective of the DB Magistrate which could have been cool. But it really doesn't read that way, it is a story where the DB Magistrate seem to be pretty clearly the protagonist, you get a picture of her motivations, drive, and beliefs...but then you never get to see her act like the protagonist she was set up to be, the story just ends with the bland generic solar swooping in and taking all the momentum of the story for himself...which Is a problem because I don't know who the heck he is or why I should care about him.<br /> <br /> Part of me is like, this is ostensibly the &quot;Solar&quot; book so yes they should seem to be potent when they show up in the fiction. But the other non-Solar splats featured in the fiction were given a chance to shine on their own, and not be second fiddle to Solars, so it's kinda a shame that the same didn't really happen for DB. I'm just hoping that in &quot;DB: What Fire Has Wrought&quot; where the chapter fiction is going to be much more DB focused they wont have their protagonist status usurped by the other splats quite as much. It ain't easy being a terrestrial...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:28:25-08:00","id":771297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771234#post771234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the guys trying to kill me are planning on taking an army to my homeland, burn it to the ground and kill it's people...no, not really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the Great Houses; that's not their plan, not really. But their plan <i>is</i> to murder the magistrates and such now that the protection granted by the Empress is evaporating like shadows at noontime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T01:47:02-08:00","id":771325,"title":"","content":"Is it <i>possible</i> that somebody saying &quot;this is not the Realm you swore to protect&quot; and &quot;let us [...] put things right&quot; might be somebody at least acting like they support the existence of the Realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:55:50-08:00","id":771396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771297#post771297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the Great Houses; that's not their plan, not really. But their plan <i>is</i> to murder the magistrates and such now that the protection granted by the Empress is evaporating like shadows at noontime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but joining forces with a prince of hell and aiding their conquest of your home seems like a pretty thoughtless overreaction. I'd be pretty pissed if my government tried to have me assassinated but I'm not going to run off and help ISIS launch an invasion of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771325#post771325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it <i>possible</i> that somebody saying &amp;quot;this is not the Realm you swore to protect&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;let us [...] put things right&amp;quot; might be somebody at least acting like they support the existence of the Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I got from it at all, but if that's what's going on then it's way better. Pretending to want to purge the Realm of corruption would actually be a fantastic way of getting a magistrate to do whatever you want them to do, and would simultaneously be a great agent to have on the Blessed Isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T05:19:40-08:00","id":771410,"title":"","content":"Pretending?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T05:49:36-08:00","id":771423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771410#post771410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretending?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't get the feeling that he was pretending from that. I mean, I am in agreement that it is perhaps not the best written story that could be, but I do feel it's not <i>necessarily</i> something that sees her as a gullible fool. It's my feeling that she probably did turn, especially if she's already been attacked by the Great Houses - the Realm is no longer what it was in the Empress' time, and her checks on the power of the Houses are crumbling. I can see magistrates who genuinely believed in the Realm as a stabilizing and civilizing influence leaving what once was in favor of the resurgent Solars, particularly if doubts have been eating at them for however many years.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's not <i>much</i> evidence of that in the text, but I think it can reasonably be extrapolated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T02:02:35-08:00","id":772164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=771171#post771171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to struggle to find a story of a character switching sides in the heat of the moment that isn't really contrived.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is very true, so put one in their for the DB that have always struggled in the setting with being the Solars whipping post, especially after many long threads on this board, and rpg.net over the years about how the DB appear in the setting.<br /> <br /> Its a bad choice of story for the DB that really doesn't fill me with hope for the splat, I am possibly over sensitive as DB are my favorite and don't feel they have ever been treated very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:44:52-08:00","id":773393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=772164#post772164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a bad choice of story for the DB that really doesn't fill me with hope for the splat, I am possibly over sensitive as DB are my favorite and don't feel they have ever been treated very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm overly sensitive too, and I freely admit it, even though I hate being so defensive.. I just really want them to have concrete motivations for their actions in this editions rather than, &quot;Lol powerstruggle.&quot; Otherwise they seem even more self-destructive than First Age Solars and that's really, really not their characterization.<br /> <br /> As it said in the stuff about the Balorian Crusade, even dying of plague the Dragonblooded charged out to fight the enemies of Creaton, and held them back far longer than anyone could have imagined, even as they died in droves. THAT'S what Dragonblooded should be about, not &quot;My neighbor and I were having a petty squabble over Jade and then a Dawn strolled by and cleft us in twain with his mighty daiklave.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8946-lonesome-akuma","name":"Lonesome Akuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:53:11-08:00","id":773400,"title":"","content":"I'd wait for the Dragon-Blooded book before making a complete judgement on how the fiction is treating the splat, even if some concerns are entirely valid right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:55:01-08:00","id":773404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773400#post773400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wait for the Dragon-Blooded book before making a complete judgement on how the fiction is treating the splat, even if some concerns are entirely valid right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Let us pray it takes a shorter devcycle than the Core book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8946-lonesome-akuma","name":"Lonesome Akuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:26:41-08:00","id":773586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lonesome Akuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773404#post773404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. Let us pray it takes a shorter devcycle than the Core book!</div> </div> </div> </div>At least the writing is basically done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:32:21-08:00","id":773732,"title":"","content":"While I agree DBs got shafted to a large degree (mechanically, and somewhat narratively), I also find it strange that people identify with an underdog...and then complain when they really are underdogs.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema are Chtulu. If someone solos Chtulu, he's not really Cthulu anymore. So yeah, I expect DBs to lose most of the time in fair fights.<br /> <br /> Which is why DBs never fight fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:56:19-08:00","id":773746,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between being the underdog and being butt-floss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T02:14:33-08:00","id":773755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=772164#post772164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is very true, so put one in their for the DB that have always struggled in the setting with being the Solars whipping post, especially after many long threads on this board, and rpg.net over the years about how the DB appear in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had a thought, I don't have a point to make with it at all, but how funny would it be if there was a story about a magistrate who punched a Twilight in the face and said &quot;Join the Realm, it's the winning side, and help use it's power to make the world a better place.&quot; and he totally went for it. Like he just went right from there to building a special divining rod to help them find and kill other Solars because he wholeheartedly supported the Empire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773732#post773732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree DBs got shafted to a large degree (mechanically, and somewhat narratively), I also find it strange that people identify with an underdog...and then complain when they really are underdogs.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema are Chtulu. If someone solos Chtulu, he's not really Cthulu anymore. So yeah, I expect DBs to lose most of the time in fair fights.<br /> <br /> Which is why DBs never fight fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the Solars supposed to be the underdog heroes? They're the ones with no backing or support fighting against an empire that could lose 1,000 soldiers and go &quot;Meh.&quot;. You're supposed to be Luke Skywalker* in the rebellion, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm so sorry for all the Star Wars metaphors but I can't help it. NEXT MONTH!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T02:48:00-08:00","id":773768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773755#post773755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Solars supposed to be the underdog heroes? They're the ones with no backing or support fighting against an empire that could lose 1,000 soldiers and go &quot;Meh.&quot;. You're supposed to be Luke Skywalker* in the rebellion, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm so sorry for all the Star Wars metaphors but I can't help it. NEXT MONTH!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Exalted violates some genre conventions on that one. On a large scale, yes, the Solars are the underdogs. The Realm is the Empire, with all the territory, infrastructure, troops, etc. The Solars have themselves and whatever ragtag forces they put together. That largely follows standard Sci-Fi/Fantasy convention.<br /> <br /> On the personal side, though, the dynamic is completely flipped. Solars are Darth Vader, and Dragon-Bloods are Luke. If you white-roomed the Vader/Luke fight (and we love our white rooms) Luke loses 99/100 times. He gets to win based on the story. Which is fine.<br /> <br /> So, Exalted violates some expectations along the way, but the net result is two PC Exalts with a fun, dynamic play experience. Both are challenged, and both have numerous win and fail conditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T03:03:43-08:00","id":773780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773732#post773732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema are Chtulu.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema are Heracles or Odysseus or Polyphemus or the Monkey King; it's preferable to employ some manner of unexpected tactic than to directly engage them in their area of greatest strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773732#post773732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone solos Chtulu, he's not really Cthulu anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a reminder, Cthulhu (which is how it's spelled) was &quot;solo'ed&quot; by one guy (driving a steamship through his head).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-25-2015, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:03:57-08:00","id":773832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773780#post773780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a reminder, Cthulhu (which is how it's spelled) was &quot;solo'ed&quot; by one guy (driving a steamship through his head).</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth I read that story a little while ago and Cthulhu immediately starts to reform after said steam ship gets driven through his head. I mean, I know Holden is quoted as saying that Cthulhu is a bitch in exalted terms* because he couldn't take a turn of the century steam ship to the face, but that's 250 tones of solid steel smacking him right in the noggin and it just made him dizzy for a little while.<br /> <br /> *yes I know it was a joke","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:20:04-08:00","id":773843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773832#post773832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth I read that story a little while ago and Cthulhu immediately starts to reform after said steam ship gets driven through his head. I mean, I know Holden is quoted as saying that Cthulhu is a bitch in exalted terms* because he couldn't take a turn of the century steam ship to the face, but that's 250 tones of solid steel smacking him right in the noggin and it just made him dizzy for a little while.<br /> <br /> *yes I know it was a joke</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't kill him, true, but he didn't get up from it afterward. There's a parallel to be drawn here, with Juggernaut. Does the fact that they didn't kill him cause the First Age Exalted to have not beaten him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:56:21-08:00","id":773861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773843#post773843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't kill him, true, but he didn't get up from it afterward. There's a parallel to be drawn here, with Juggernaut. Does the fact that they didn't kill him cause the First Age Exalted to have not beaten him?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to say, given the crazy stuff that went on in the First Age. I could be that he couldn't be destroyed/killed, so had to be magically imprisoned or whatever. Equally, he might not have even been a huge threat and might have ended up just being shoved into wherever he was found along with more serious threats. There's a lot of room for STs to decide there.<br /> <br /> It's not quite like Cthulhu because Cthulhu was momentarily inconvenienced. It's a bit like bear-spraying a Solar, running away, him not being able to find you, and you considering that a victory (which fair enough, in a way it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T06:06:19-08:00","id":773870,"title":"","content":"Actually, if one <i>wants</i> to force the &quot;Solars are Cthulhu&quot; analogy (I don't, but some of y'all seem interested in that), one could point out that by the strictures of the Immaculate Philosophy, the Solars slain by the Wyld Hunt are only ever put down for as long as it takes them to possess someone again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T04:53:01-08:00","id":777089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/456427-exalted-fiction-and-dragon-blooded?p=773780#post773780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema are Heracles or Odysseus or Polyphemus or the Monkey King; it's preferable to employ some manner of unexpected tactic than to directly engage them in their area of greatest strength.<br /> <br /> As a reminder, Cthulhu (which is how it's spelled) was &quot;solo'ed&quot; by one guy (driving a steamship through his head).</div> </div> </div> </div>You say Cthulhu, I say Cthulu. Within the story, his name is unutterable by the human tongue. Feel better?<br /> <br /> As for the steamer line, yes, Alucard, I read the story, along with a great deal of Lovecraft's other work. You have to ground it within the time-frame it was written. We live in a world of mecha and Godzilla and Exalted. We live in a world where the power of the atomic weapon is conceptually easy to grasp. From the standpoint of the audience and the writer, the idea that <i>anything</i> could take that kind of impact to the face and live was existentially terrifying. Worse, that the thing had just woken up, and <i>will </i>come back. He's a creature for whom death is a temporary condition<br /> <br /> That's really the kind of threat the Anathema pose to the Dragon-Blooded. If caught while they are young, Anathema can be &quot;killed,&quot; but they will return. If allowed to grow in power, they can become monstrously difficult to destroy. And their destruction may require the use of terrible First Age weapons, or tramp steamers (you don't generally need to ram a person with a ship to kill them).<br /> <br /> That isn't intended to oversell Celestials mechanically, but rather to emphasize how terrifying they are from the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded who fight them. A Dynast who faces off against a Lunar in the Threshold with his buddies is fighting the boogeyman, that thing he has been taught from birth to fear and hate. It's incredibly heroic and brave to stand and fight to the death rather than running. If one or two of his sworn brothers die, that's just the cost that was paid to keep Creation safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T07:30:06-08:00","id":777752,"title":"","content":"Hah, Totentanz, your last sentence remind me of the old &quot;White Man's Burden&quot; poem as a way to illustrate the DB's worldview.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Take up the White Man's burden, Send forth the best ye breed</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Go bind your sons to exile, to serve your captives' need;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">To wait in heavy harness, On fluttered folk and wild\u2014</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Your new-caught, sullen peoples, Half-devil and half-child.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> No doubt some of their apologists and propagandists see it as their charge and thus &quot;burden&quot; - to send &quot;the best they breed&quot; to &quot;exile&quot; and possible death in the Threshold to protect the ungrateful, unenlightened people whom they have conquered. It fits their viewpoint quite well, indeed - including how it looks from the other side.<br /> <br /> Anywho, I agree with the viewpoint that Solars, especially at the start, should be very dangerous to Dragon-blooded and small groups, but not impossibly so. A veteran dragonblooded warrior should be a very, very dangerous challenge to a starting warrior solar, and someone a less martially oriented starting character should try to engage on other terms (or just, you know, stay away from for the time being).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 12-01-2015, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}